    "text_leads": [
      {
        "key": "contract_assets",
        "label": "Unbilled revenue / contract assets",
        "excerpt": ", Financial Instruments — Credit Losses (Topic 326): Measurement of Credit Losses for Accounts Receivable and Contract Assets Issued July 30, 2025 The FASB issued ASU 2025-05, introducing a practical expedient and policy election for estimating expected credit losses on c",
        "classification": "unverified_text_lead",
        "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1474167/000147793226005146/cosm_10q.htm",
        "accession": "0001477932-26-005146",
        "form": "10-Q",
        "filed": "2026-08-18"
      },
      {
        "key": "variable_consideration",
        "label": "Variable consideration / rebates / returns",
        "excerpt": "e of nutraceutical products, the Company determined that the transaction price for sales to Medihelm includes variable consideration. In accordance with ASC 606, Revenue from Contracts with Customers, and specifically ASC 606-10-32-5, the Company applies the \"expected value\" method",
        "classification": "unverified_text_lead",
        "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1474167/000147793226005146/cosm_10q.htm",
        "accession": "0001477932-26-005146",
        "form": "10-Q",
        "filed": "2026-08-18"
      },
      {
        "key": "related_party_sales",
        "label": "Related-party revenue",
        "excerpt": "OSMOS HEALTH INC. Notes to Unaudited Condensed Consolidated Financial Statements June 30, 2026 NOTE 9 – RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS Doc Pharma S.A. Doc Pharma S.A. is considered a related party to the Company due to the fact that the CEO of Doc Pharma is the son of Grigorios S",
        "classification": "unverified_text_lead",
        "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1474167/000147793226005146/cosm_10q.htm",
        "accession": "0001477932-26-005146",
        "form": "10-Q",
        "filed": "2026-08-18"
      },
      {
        "key": "significant_financing",
        "label": "Significant financing component",
        "excerpt": "practical expedient available for its trade receivables, which are short-term in nature and do not contain a significant financing component. The Company applies a loss-rate method for calculating expected credit losses (“ECL”) on accounts receivable, based on a combination of historical e",
        "classification": "unverified_text_lead",
        "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1474167/000147793226005146/cosm_10q.htm",
        "accession": "0001477932-26-005146",
        "form": "10-Q",
        "filed": "2026-08-18"
      },
      {
        "key": "deferred_revenue",
        "label": "Deferred revenue / contract liabilities",
        "excerpt": "tively, are included in “Other Current Liabilities” in accordance with ASC 606-10-45-2 (Revenue Recognition – Contract Liabilities). Approximately $ 1.4 million of the June 30, 2026 balance relates to deferred revenue recorded in connection with uncollected amounts from Medihelm",
        "classification": "unverified_text_lead",
        "source_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1474167/000147793226005146/cosm_10q.htm",
        "accession": "0001477932-26-005146",
